# This repo has core.autocrlf=true and no .gitattributes at the root, so a
# plain `git checkout` on Windows silently rewrites every LF in a tracked text
# file to CRLF in the working tree -- and `git status`/`git diff` report no
# change, because git's comparison normalizes line endings before comparing.
#
# That is fatal to this directory specifically: the whole point of
# vectors/*.json is byte-exact reproducibility -- committed SHA-256 digests,
# `ends_with_newline` assertions, and byte-for-byte bundle regeneration checks.
# It actually happened here on 2026-08-19, after an ordinary branch-switch-and-
# merge sequence, and vectors/manifest.json's "CRLF corruption" note has the
# full story, including that services/cve/snapshot/ has the identical exposure
# and was not fixed (out of scope for this task).
#
# `-text` disables line-ending translation in BOTH directions, on every
# platform, for every file below -- not `text eol=lf`, which would still run
# git's normalization machinery and just aim it at LF; `-text` means git never
# touches these bytes at all, which is what "byte-exact" actually requires.
vectors/*.json -text
